    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456-a1">

                <pb facs="0548" n="468" xml:id="pg468"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Lansdowne to Mr.
                            Choate</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: The Marquis of Salisbury
                    referred your letter of the 25th ultimo to the secretary of state for war, and I
                    have now the honor to inform your excellency that a telegram has been received
                    from the military authorities in Ceylon to the effect that there is no objection
                    to the United States consul at Colombo communicating with the 22 prisoners of
                    war referred to in your excellency’s note, but that all communications should be
                    made either through the governor of Ceylon or through the general officer
                    commanding the troops.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansdowne</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
